argus-scanner (1.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Use tomli for TOML configuration files on Python 3.10 (tomllib exists
    from 3.11 only).  This fixes suppression lists and project config on
    the minimum supported interpreter.
  * Declare tomli as a conditional dependency in pyproject.toml.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the binary package architecture independent (Architecture: all,
    about 300 kB).  The wheel set is no longer vendored: the package ships
    only the pure-Python argus wheel, and the runtime is built during
    installation, so it always matches the local architecture and Python ABI.
  * Install the latest Semgrep from PyPI when the package is configured,
    which removes the need to rebuild the package for every Semgrep release.
  * Replace argus-update-semgrep with argus-setup-runtime: it provisions,
    upgrades, pins, lists and removes the runtime, and supports offline
    installation from a wheel directory.
  * Raise the Python requirement to 3.10, matching current Semgrep releases.
  * Drop the vendored-wheel exception to Debian Policy 4.13: the source
    package no longer contains third-party binaries.
  * Remove the pip-managed Semgrep environment used by 1.1.0-2 on upgrade.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fetch the latest Semgrep from PyPI on first installation so the rule
    engine can be updated independently of the package.  The bundled copy
    remains as a fallback; the download is best-effort and an offline
    installation still succeeds.
  * Add argus-update-semgrep to install, upgrade, pin or remove that copy,
    including offline installation from a wheel directory.
  * Depend on python3-venv for the isolated Semgrep environment.
  * Remove the pip-managed environment on purge.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package.
  * Bundle the Python dependency closure in a private runtime because
    python3-tree-sitter, python3-tree-sitter-java and Semgrep are not
    available in the Debian archive.

